    "institutions_today": [],
    "paragraph": "\"Energysheds and the Urban Energy Transition: A Method for Assessing Spatial Imbalances in Energy Flow\" introduces an energyshed-based method to map spatial supply and demand relationships between urban energy-consuming areas and power generation facilities. \"Transit-Oriented Land Use Planning Using Deep Reinforcement Learning\" presents DRL4TOD, a deep reinforcement learning framework that uses graph neural networks to model spatial relationships between land parcels, road networks, and metro stations for assigning land-use types and floor area ratios. \"Foundation-Model Residuals as Signals of Urban Bus Irregularity\" analyzes spatial and travel-time prediction errors from UniTraj and TrajFM trajectory foundation models transferred to Niterói, Brazil, using the NetMob26 dataset.",
